# Pulsar preamble — print start
#
# Paste at the top of a Grasshopper-emitted print program, immediately
# after the lib_pulsar.script function defs. Connects to the Duet, clears
# heater faults, blocks until both zones are at temp, then starts the
# extrusion daemon. After this block returns, the screw is turning and
# the daemon is auto-topping-up the queue.
#
# Temps below are PLA. For PETG try barrel=220, nozzle=245.

duet_open("172.22.22.100", 23)

if (duet_handshake(2.0) == False):
  popup("ERROR: Duet did not respond to M115. Aborting.")
  halt
end

pulsar_clear_heater_faults()
pulsar_preheat(190, 215)
pulsar_start_extrusion(900, 100)
